  "notes": "{和|やわ}らげる is the transitive form, meaning to actively soften or ease something.\n\nVERB TYPE:\n- Ichidan verb (る-verb)\n- Transitive\n- Intransitive pair: {和|やわ}らぐ\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {痛|いた}みを{和|やわ}らげる (to ease pain)\n- {緊張|きんちょう}を{和|やわ}らげる (to ease tension)\n- {衝撃|しょうげき}を{和|やわ}らげる (to soften impact)\n- {表現|ひょうげん}を{和|やわ}らげる (to soften expression)\n- {口調|くちょう}を{和|やわ}らげる (to soften one's tone)\n- {雰囲気|ふんいき}を{和|やわ}らげる (to ease the atmosphere)\n\nINTRANSITIVE PAIR:\n- {和|やわ}らぐ: Something softens on its own\n- {和|やわ}らげる: Someone actively softens something\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {和|やわ}らぐ (intransitive: to ease, soften)\n- {緩和|かんわ}する (to alleviate - formal)\n- {軽減|けいげん}する (to reduce - formal)\n- {落|お}ち{着|つ}かせる (to calm down - transitive)\n\nREGISTER: Neutral to slightly formal. Common in everyday use.",
